apps/mobile/build/
apps/mobile/.packages
# pubspec.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. This is an application, not a
# reusable package, so the lockfile belongs in git. Shorebird also requires a
# patch build to produce native output identical to the release it patches --
# unpinned, `flutter pub get` resolves newer transitive deps, which shifts the
# R8/DEX output and makes every patch fail with "your app contains native
# changes". That cost us two patches before we traced it here.

